---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Draft from '../components/Draft.astro';
import { updated } from '../data/dates';

const timeline = [
  ['July 2018', 'Opens as an Akron Public Schools school with 240 students in grades 3 and 4, chosen by lottery from students in the bottom 30% in reading.'],
  ['April 2019', 'District testing (NWEA MAP) shows 90% of students met or exceeded their expected growth in reading and math.'],
  ['2018-19', "Ohio's report card gives the school an A for progress but an F for achievement. Performance index: 53.5."],
  ['2019-20', 'The pandemic closes schools. No state tests are given.'],
  ['2020-21', 'Performance index falls to 27.5.'],
  ['2021-22', 'Performance index recovers to 38. The school has lost its founding principal and gone through three interim principals in about a year and a half.'],
  ['2023', 'About 11% of the first eighth-grade class is proficient on the state English test, and the class had not passed the state math test since third grade.'],
];

const sources = [
  ['LeBron James Family Foundation, "Promising Results" (Apr 2019)', 'https://lebronjamesfamilyfoundation.org/news/promising-results'],
  ['CBS Sports, first-year test score gains (Apr 2019)', 'https://www.cbssports.com/nba/news/lebron-james-i-promise-school-sees-extraordinary-test-score-improvement-after-first-year'],
  ['Thomas B. Fordham Institute, "An in-depth analysis of the I Promise School\'s troubling academic results" (Aug 2023)', 'https://fordhaminstitute.org/ohio/commentary/depth-analysis-i-promise-schools-troubling-academic-results'],
  ['FOX 4, reporting on Akron Beacon Journal coverage of 2023 test results (Jul 2023)', 'https://www.fox4news.com/news/lebron-james-backed-i-promise-school-delivers-discouraging-student-test-results-report'],
  ['I Promise School', 'https://ipromise.school/'],
];
---

<Base title="Lessons from Akron · We Promise" description="What the Akron I Promise School got right, where results fell short, and what Newark should do differently.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Lessons learned</p>
  <h1>What Akron teaches us</h1>
  <Draft updated={updated.lessons} note="A starting point for the research and lessons seat. Results after 2023 still need to be pulled from Ohio's school report cards." />

  <p class="page-intro">
    The Foundation will know the Akron story better than anyone, including the hard parts. A credible
    pitch names them and shows how Newark plans for them.
  </p>

  <p class="callout">
    The short version: families and students got real support, and early growth was strong. But
    proficiency stayed low, the pandemic hit hard, and leadership turned over. Newark should keep the
    supports and build the academic plan and the leadership bench just as carefully.
  </p>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>What happened in Akron</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="data">
        <thead><tr><th>When</th><th>What happened</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{timeline.map(([w, t]) => <tr><td><strong>{w}</strong></td><td>{t}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="small">
      Ohio's performance index gives zero credit for students who are not tested, which pulls down
      pandemic-era scores. Statewide and district scores also fell during those years.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>What worked</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card"><h3>Whole-family support</h3><p>The Family Resource Center offers GED prep, job help, and health and legal services, treating parents as part of the school.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Removing barriers</h3><p>Counseling, a food pantry, clothing, tutoring, housing help, free uniforms and bikes, and University of Akron tuition for graduates.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Early growth</h3><p>In the first year most students grew faster than expected, starting from far behind. Growth earned an A on the state report card.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>More time</h3><p>A longer school day and year are built into the model from the start.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Where it fell short</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card short"><h3>Proficiency</h3><p>Growth did not become grade-level results. Few students reached proficiency in reading or math by eighth grade.</p></div>
      <div class="card short"><h3>Leadership churn</h3><p>The founding principal left in year three, followed by three interim principals in about a year and a half.</p></div>
      <div class="card short"><h3>The pandemic</h3><p>A school built around in-person time and family contact lost both in its second and third years.</p></div>
      <div class="card short"><h3>Cost versus results</h3><p>Critics noted that the extra money, time and services should have shown up in scores. There is no public cost-effectiveness study.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>What Newark does differently</h2>
    <ol class="prose">
      <li><strong>Set academic targets on day one.</strong> Publish goals for both growth and proficiency, by grade, and report them every year. The <a href="/plan/#pathway">Promise Pathway</a> makes those goals visible to each child.</li>
      <li><strong>Hire an outside evaluator from the start.</strong> The <a href="/budget/">budget</a> funds data and evaluation every year, so results are measured independently and not only by the district.</li>
      <li><strong>Build a leadership bench.</strong> Name a successor plan for the principal and the program director before opening, and budget for retention.</li>
      <li><strong>Make the academic plan as strong as the supports.</strong> Wraparound services open the door; a proven reading and math program has to walk students through it.</li>
      <li><strong>Plan for disruption.</strong> Have a written plan for keeping tutoring, meals and family contact going if school is interrupted.</li>
      <li><strong>Ask Akron directly.</strong> Visit the I Promise team and ask what they would change. That conversation is step two of the <a href="/pitch/">pitch</a>.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Still to research</h2>
    <ul class="prose">
      <li>Ohio report card results for 2022-23 through 2024-25.</li>
      <li>Attendance and chronic absence compared with similar Akron schools.</li>
      <li>Family Resource Center use and parent outcomes (GED, jobs).</li>
      <li>The Foundation's and district's actual annual spending per student.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <ul class="small">
      {sources.map(([t, u]) => <li><a href={u}>{t}</a></li>)}
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .short { border-top: 5px solid var(--brick); }
  .card:not(.short) { border-top: 5px solid #13917f; }
</style>
